        'The Scientific-Technical Council develops and implements the strategy for the university\'s scientific, technical, research, and organizational activity. Its tasks include organizing fundamental and applied research in technical, natural-science, and socio-humanitarian fields; building partnerships with international funds, industrial enterprises, and research centers; strengthening methods for involving students in the research process and coordinating their research work; and promoting the university\'s scientific achievements through exhibitions and publishing services.',
        'The university runs two research institutes — "Ecology and Biology" and "Pedagogy and Psychology."',
